o bicycles in the sculpture without indicating that they are fused together or describing how they are fused. Choice D is incorrect. It identifies the artist who created the sculpture but doesn&rsquo;t describe how the bicycles are fused together.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061192,"updateDate":1755117061192}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061192, 1755117061192),
    ($SATQ$00e0170f$SATQ$, $SATQ$4a0e7481-a0e1-4b5c-9fde-d9ecfa15f63f$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$fde0d8a2-8125-4c6b-880a-1f58fa11cad8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Magnetic levitation (maglev) trains are suspended above a track by powerful electromagnets, reducing friction and thus allowing for much faster speeds. Though maglev advocates in the US have long imagined these trains crisscrossing the country, their dream remains unrealized. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> of the handful of maglev trains currently in operation, all are in Asia.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"48969ed7-b497-41df-a551-14cdc4e32b8a","content":"<p>In fact,</p>"},{"id":"4dc1955e-d6d1-49fe-8d84-ff00172bb9e3","content":"<p>To that end,</p>"},{"id":"20b32df7-ee6a-40ba-b226-f83fa098709c","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"c8510328-773e-4990-80e4-661744d548f4","content":"<p>That said,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["48969ed7-b497-41df-a551-14cdc4e32b8a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. This sentence emphasizes just how far maglev advocates&rsquo; dreams are from coming true. &ldquo;In fact&rdquo; is a transition used to emphasize the truth of a statement that modifies the previous statement and therefore fits perfectly in this context. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice uses a cause-and-effect transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Maglev advocates&rsquo; dream remaining unrealized would not cause there to be only a few maglev trains, all located in Asia. Choice C is incorrect. This choice uses a disagreement transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. In fact, this sentence agrees with the previous sentence&mdash;both talk about how maglev trains are far from becoming common in the US. Choice D is incorrect. This choice uses a disagreement transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. In fact, this sentence agrees with the previous sentence&mdash;both talk about how maglev trains are far from becoming common in the US. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TRA-H010$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$56e8967a-3bd7-43c5-813d-e3598dceced1$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"00e0170f","external_id":"4a0e7481-a0e1-4b5c-9fde-d9ecfa15f63f","vaultid":"fde0d8a2-8125-4c6b-880a-1f58fa11cad8","uId":"79287017-b6f9-48ac-9d47-b18857a9c149","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Magnetic levitation (maglev) trains are suspended above a track by powerful electromagnets, reducing friction and thus allowing for much faster speeds. Though maglev advocates in the US have long imagined these trains crisscrossing the country, their dream remains unrealized. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> of the handful of maglev trains currently in operation, all are in Asia.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"48969ed7-b497-41df-a551-14cdc4e32b8a","content":"<p>In fact,</p>"},{"id":"4dc1955e-d6d1-49fe-8d84-ff00172bb9e3","content":"<p>To that end,</p>"},{"id":"20b32df7-ee6a-40ba-b226-f83fa098709c","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"c8510328-773e-4990-80e4-661744d548f4","content":"<p>That said,</p>"}],"keys":["48969ed7-b497-41df-a551-14cdc4e32b8a"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. This sentence emphasizes just how far maglev advocates&rsquo; dreams are from coming true. &ldquo;In fact&rdquo; is a transition used to emphasize the truth of a statement that modifies the previous statement and therefore fits perfectly in this context. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice uses a cause-and-effect transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Maglev advocates&rsquo; dream remaining unrealized would not cause there to be only a few maglev trains, all located in Asia. Choice C is incorrect. This choice uses a disagreement transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. In fact, this sentence agrees with the previous sentence&mdash;both talk about how maglev trains are far from becoming common in the US. Choice D is incorrect. This choice uses a disagreement transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. In fact, this sentence agrees with the previous sentence&mdash;both talk about how maglev trains are far from becoming common in the US. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TRA-H010","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"56e8967a-3bd7-43c5-813d-e3598dceced1","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959373,"updateDate":1691007959373}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959373, 1691007959373),
    ($SATQ$01c8c433$SATQ$, $SATQ$e8ec1e19-db4a-4a21-9b50-cde422127a67$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$19b7136a-56ee-4d04-a1c1-633703779bb4$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Before the 1847 introduction of the US postage stamp, the cost of postage was usually paid by the recipient of a letter rather than the sender, and recipients were not always able or willing to pay promptly. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> collecting this fee could be slow and arduous, and heaps of unpaid-for, undeliverable mail piled up in post offices.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4a63b89f-f34d-49d1-b773-a4e2bd18d166","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"},{"id":"b559ca3c-089b-4eea-b3b7-3887e139e6b9","content":"<p>On the contrary,</p>"},{"id":"68692570-648e-48e1-8518-5daf319a8dd0","content":"<p>Consequently,</p>"},{"id":"54f4391b-d361-4969-9f45-a7a9f4516e3b","content":"<p>For example,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["68692570-648e-48e1-8518-5daf319a8dd0"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;Consequently&rdquo; logically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence (slow fee collection, heaps of undeliverable mail) were a consequence of the fee system described in the previous sentence. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;regardless&rdquo; illogically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence occurred despite the fee system described in the previous sentence. Instead, they were a consequence of that system. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;on the contrary&rdquo; illogically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence contrast with the fee system described in the previous sentence. Instead, they were a consequence of that system. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;for example&rdquo; illogically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence are an example of the fee system described in the previous sentence. Instead, they were a consequence of that system. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TRA-M001$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$84cc0150-662e-413c-875c-fb63e78b8f9b$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"01c8c433","external_id":"e8ec1e19-db4a-4a21-9b50-cde422127a67","vaultid":"19b7136a-56ee-4d04-a1c1-633703779bb4","uId":"220b3544-01ed-42e0-9a30-25e93a4a9616","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Before the 1847 introduction of the US postage stamp, the cost of postage was usually paid by the recipient of a letter rather than the sender, and recipients were not always able or willing to pay promptly. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> collecting this fee could be slow and arduous, and heaps of unpaid-for, undeliverable mail piled up in post offices.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"4a63b89f-f34d-49d1-b773-a4e2bd18d166","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"},{"id":"b559ca3c-089b-4eea-b3b7-3887e139e6b9","content":"<p>On the contrary,</p>"},{"id":"68692570-648e-48e1-8518-5daf319a8dd0","content":"<p>Consequently,</p>"},{"id":"54f4391b-d361-4969-9f45-a7a9f4516e3b","content":"<p>For example,</p>"}],"keys":["68692570-648e-48e1-8518-5daf319a8dd0"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;Consequently&rdquo; logically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence (slow fee collection, heaps of undeliverable mail) were a consequence of the fee system described in the previous sentence. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;regardless&rdquo; illogically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence occurred despite the fee system described in the previous sentence. Instead, they were a consequence of that system. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;on the contrary&rdquo; illogically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence contrast with the fee system described in the previous sentence. Instead, they were a consequence of that system. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;for example&rdquo; illogically signals that the postal problems described in this sentence are an example of the fee system described in the previous sentence. Instead, they were a consequence of that system. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TRA-M001","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"84cc0150-662e-413c-875c-fb63e78b8f9b","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959373,"updateDate":1691007959373}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959373, 1691007959373),
    ($SATQ$0205e563$SATQ$, $SATQ$361cfad2-26f4-4227-886d-d6f8b8d7147a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$f9b5b523-7927-4efc-8531-64ec4f6f1d36$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>At two weeks old, the time their critical socialization period begins, wolves can smell but cannot yet see or hear. Domesticated dogs, <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> can see, hear, and smell by the end of two weeks. This relative lack of sensory input may help explain why wolves behave so differently around humans than dogs do: from a very young age, wolves are more wary and less exploratory.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f40a8510-97cd-4686-abaa-1ee3758e2ed0","content":"<p>in other words,</p>"},{"id":"2d4645ca-f739-46e5-b64c-f9633cdfe673","content":"<p>for instance,</p>"},{"id":"16e641c9-0080-4b9c-84a2-0ab55dfcf9e5","content":"<p>by contrast,</p>"},{"id":"ac71ba3f-0a08-45b7-a079-6b0855768de8","content":"<p>accordingly,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["16e641c9-0080-4b9c-84a2-0ab55dfcf9e5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;By contrast&rdquo; logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that dogs can see, hear, and smell by the end of two weeks&mdash;contrasts with the preceding information (that wolves can smell but not see or hear at the same age). </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;in other words&rdquo; illogically signals that the information about domesticated dogs in this sentence paraphrases the information about wolves in the previous sentence. Instead, the information about dogs contrasts with what came before. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;for instance&rdquo; illogically signals that the information about domesticated dogs in this sentence exemplifies the information about wolves in the previous sentence. Instead, the information about dogs contrasts with what came before. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;accordingly&rdquo; illogically signals that the information about domesticated dogs in this sentence is in accordance with, or results from, the information about wolves in the previous sentence. Instead, the information about dogs contrasts with what came before. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-214-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$34ae1e9f-c5b1-4163-b77f-8eaf257f37ab$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"0205e563","external_id":"361cfad2-26f4-4227-886d-d6f8b8d7147a","vaultid":"f9b5b523-7927-4efc-8531-64ec4f6f1d36","uId":"f4c9ae96-9dad-445a-bcf1-bcfd2700c761","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>At two weeks old, the time their critical socialization period begins, wolves can smell but cannot yet see or hear. Domesticated dogs, <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> can see, hear, and smell by the end of two weeks. This relative lack of sensory input may help explain why wolves behave so differently around humans than dogs do: from a very young age, wolves are more wary and less exploratory.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f40a8510-97cd-4686-abaa-1ee3758e2ed0","content":"<p>in other words,</p>"},{"id":"2d4645ca-f739-46e5-b64c-f9633cdfe673","content":"<p>for instance,</p>"},{"id":"16e641c9-0080-4b9c-84a2-0ab55dfcf9e5","content":"<p>by contrast,</p>"},{"id":"ac71ba3f-0a08-45b7-a079-6b0855768de8","content":"<p>accordingly,</p>"}],"keys":["16e641c9-0080-4b9c-84a2-0ab55dfcf9e5"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;By contrast&rdquo; logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that dogs can see, hear, and smell by the end of two weeks&mdash;contrasts with the preceding information (that wolves can smell but not see or hear at the same age). </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;in other words&rdquo; illogically signals that the information about domesticated dogs in this sentence paraphrases the information about wolves in the previous sentence. Instead, the information about dogs contrasts with what came before. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;for instance&rdquo; illogically signals that the information about domesticated dogs in this sentence exemplifies the information about wolves in the previous sentence. Instead, the information about dogs contrasts with what came before. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;accordingly&rdquo; illogically signals that the information about domesticated dogs in this sentence is in accordance with, or results from, the information about wolves in the previous sentence. Instead, the information about dogs contrasts with what came before. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-214-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"34ae1e9f-c5b1-4163-b77f-8eaf257f37ab","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959327,"updateDate":1691007959327}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959327, 1691007959327)
